      "seed": 2045836279,
      "version": 543,
      "versionNonce": 411631897,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1762611864038,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hibernate-ORM for Java \n\n->We have studied JDBC which is a api to \nconnect  our Java application to a database\nbut after connecting our Java application to the database \nwe have to write a lot of sql querries,Now as backend developer\nit essential to know database querries but suppose you are \na fresher and u dont know about sql then for that we have \nORM -Object Relation Mapper->Which skips the Sql querries and \nfocus on plain syntax to communicate with Sql  ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Hibernate-ORM for Java \n\n->We have studied JDBC which is a api to \nconnect  our Java application to a database\nbut after connecting our Java application to the database \nwe have to write a lot of sql querries,Now as backend developer\nit essential to know database querries but suppose you are \na fresher and u dont know about sql then for that we have \nORM -Object Relation Mapper->Which skips the Sql querries and \nfocus on plain syntax to communicate with Sql  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ys6gwTCuH1n4g23Hxg51n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -309.23390310290563,
      "y": 13003.68930017295,
      "width": 723.7998046875,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 906454839,
      "version": 76,
      "versionNonce": 188723641,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1762611966634,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Complete Hibernate Guide\n\nWhat is Hibernate?\n\nHibernate is an Object-Relational Mapping (ORM)\nframework for Java. It simplifies database\noperations by mapping Java objects to database\ntables automatically.\n\nSimple Explanation:\nInstead of writing SQL queries manually,\nHibernate lets you work with Java objects, and\nit handles all the database operations behind\nthe scenes.\n\nWithout Hibernate (JDBC):\nYour Code → Write SQL → JDBC → Database\n\nWith Hibernate (ORM):\nYour Code → Java Objects → Hibernate → Database",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Complete Hibernate Guide\n\nWhat is Hibernate?\n\nHibernate is an Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) framework for Java. It simplifies database operations by mapping Java objects to database tables automatically.\n\nSimple Explanation:\nInstead of writing SQL queries manually, Hibernate lets you work with Java objects, and it handles all the database operations behind the scenes.\n\nWithout Hibernate (JDBC):\nYour Code → Write SQL → JDBC → Database\n\nWith Hibernate (ORM):\nYour Code → Java Objects → Hibernate → Database",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
