      "updated": 1763131128952,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3.or we can create another class Address and mark it with annotaion @Embeddable\nand now this wont be treated as entity it will be treated as something which\nneeds to be embedded ->and we will emebed in Student or User entity class",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3.or we can create another class Address and mark it with annotaion @Embeddable\nand now this wont be treated as entity it will be treated as something which\nneeds to be embedded ->and we will emebed in Student or User entity class",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nL2qVRTN9Hli_7h0_NfPk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -408.0587517411043,
      "y": 44223.29624368231,
      "width": 726,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1144340239,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 1722548353,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763131140829,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is @Embeddable?\n@Embeddable is an annotation used to define a class whose\ninstances are embedded as part of an entity. The embeddable class\ndoesn't have its own table - its fields are stored in the entity's\ntable.\nSimple Explanation:\nInstead of creating separate tables for related data, you can\nembed that data directly into the main table.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is @Embeddable?\n@Embeddable is an annotation used to define a class whose instances are embedded as part of an entity. The embeddable class doesn't have its own table - its fields are stored in the entity's table.\nSimple Explanation:\nInstead of creating separate tables for related data, you can embed that data directly into the main table.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
