      "versionNonce": 1076689679,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763212759039,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The best example of many to many relationship is users and apartments ,suppose there is a society\ns1 and another s2 with users (u1,u2,u3 and u4) now s1 has members (u1,u2,u3) and s2 has member(u1,u3,u4)\nnow here multiple society has multiple users and multiple users has multiple society\n\nso here if we have two table",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The best example of many to many relationship is users and apartments ,suppose there is a society\ns1 and another s2 with users (u1,u2,u3 and u4) now s1 has members (u1,u2,u3) and s2 has member(u1,u3,u4)\nnow here multiple society has multiple users and multiple users has multiple society\n\nso here if we have two table",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
